'In the years 1947-1967 Britain lost all interest in its empire'
How far do you agree with this statement?

Important to define what 'lost all interest' means in the introduction. It could mean economic interests, government interest or popular interest through culture. You could use one, multiple or all three of these

I would focus on government and popular attitudes

- Government
	- Some governments were very disinterested and had different priorities e.g. domestic
	- There is perhaps some evidence of interest due to government staying in certain places (Malaya, Kenya) to try and guarantee stability.
		- They had interest but did not see direct colonisation as the way to further their interests.
		- This could be preserving of economic interests
	- General policy of decolonisation
- Popular attitudes
	- General abandonment of deferential culture. Rise of permissive society
	- various movements like Angry Young Men who cared more about Britain than fantastical imperial tales
	- Porter - apathy to empire is long standing?

